import json
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];LIB=ROOT/'assets/art-library';BASE=ROOT/'.runtime/art-library/cargo/r002';jobs=json.loads((ROOT/'.runtime/art-library/cargo/r003/current-main-jobs.json').read_text())
for extra in ['fluid-extension','loose-extension']:
 f=ROOT/'.runtime/art-library/cargo'/extra/'r001/jobs.json'
 if f.exists():jobs+=json.loads(f.read_text())
lines=['# Cargo container collection','', 'Current collection: **26 canonical designs and 47 additional finish/accessory appearances (73 native Blender assets), mixed exact revisions r001–r003; unsigned and unpublished.** r001 was rejected by visual/physical review and remains in every design history. Draft art changes no live inventory, mass, thermal, pressure, access or damage behavior.','', '[All 26 designs](cargo-collection/current/collection-board.png) · [47 additional appearances](cargo-collection/current/appearance-board.png) · [Exact source/GLB manifest](cargo-collection/current/manifest.json) · [Common-scale Blender scene](cargo-collection/r003/blender-common-scale.png) · [Actual Shipyard scale scene](cargo-collection/r003/runtime-common-scale.png)','', '## Size and capacity matrix','', 'All dimensions and statistics below are **proposed**. The original 19 rows use body/construction envelopes; the seven fluid/loose extension rows use measured occupied bounds including their hardware. Full occupied bounds and minimum hatch clearances are in each revision validation/specification. The cargo matrix uses explicit geometry variants, not uniformly scaled copies.','', '| Design | Body W × D × H (m) | Usable L | Empty kg | Payload kg | Clear hatch W × H (m) | Opening |','| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |']
for j in jobs:
 s=j['specification'];a=s['handling'];lines.append(f"| [{j['slug']} r{s['revision']:03}](designs/{j['design_id']}/DESIGN.md) | {' × '.join(f'{v:.3f}'.rstrip('0').rstrip('.') for v in s['dimensions_m'])} | {s['usable_capacity']['value']} | {s['empty_mass']['value']} | {s['payload_limit']['value']} | {a['minimum_hatch_clear_width_m']} × {a['minimum_hatch_clear_height_m']} | {a['opening']} |")
lines+=['','## Design basis and operating assumptions','','The storage sheet supplies upright crew-space crates in three visibly different sizes; the freight sheet supplies horizontal pressure/cooling/recovery pods. Pale enamel, dark indigo frames, restrained burgundy service covers, amber utility fittings and cyan status lights are shared. Exact hidden dimensions and back/underside mechanisms are authored proposals. The source’s 1 m grid label does not override the project’s 2 m interfaces.','','A nominal 1.8 m humanoid gauge with 160 mm glove blocks appears at the same scene scale. It is a dimensional review fixture, not the production animated crew rig. Small cases remain portable only at modest gross mass; handles do not imply that a fully loaded medium case is safe to carry. Large standard freight requires a clear hatch wider than a single 2 m construction bay; its local interface is a carrier/hold installation, not a normal crew door. Oversized bodies reserve a 2 × 4 m carrier footprint. Rack carriers translate size-specific corner sockets to construction bays; these are local review fixtures, not implemented snapping/handling authority.','','The main 19 designs use four 40 mm locating feet aligned to 44 mm receiver openings with 16 mm insertion; fluid/loose extensions explicitly remain one-high with no stacking interface. Stack images demonstrate **empty mechanical mating**, not certified filled-stack loads. Deck rooms reserve 150 mm handling headroom; tall or tow-equipped units are limited to one-high there. Freed cargo apertures are shown at half-open and open poses. Blender contains parented moving assemblies; the neutral visual GLB intentionally bakes their world transforms because the current Shipyard prototype loader does not preserve an arbitrary mechanical rig. No runtime opening capability is asserted.','','Usable litres are a conservative unobstructed interior envelope after frame, lid ledge and cooling-service reserve; they are not external volume or inventory slot count. Fluid litres use inner cylindrical radius, end-cap spacing and 90% fill. Refrigerated bays have a modeled divider. Empty masses are shell/frame/hardware budget allocations, and payloads are game-design targets; none are structural certification or implemented stats. Gross mass is empty container plus independently identified contents.','','| Function | Proposed operating target | Explicit limit |','| --- | --- | --- |','| Standard | Dry interior storage | No pressure rating |','| Reinforced | 1.3× standard payload target, heavier perimeter/load bands | No approved armor/health claim |','| Refrigerated | 2–8 °C; medium 70 W continuous/150 W peak, large 220/500 W | Thermal performance and loss-of-power holdover unvalidated |','| Vacuum | 100 kPa differential target | Sealed hatch geometry does not certify pressure resistance |','| Salvage | 20 kN large / 60 kN oversized tow target | No hot/reactive containment or live tractor grant |','| Medical | Clean dry supplies, 15–25 °C target | No sterile or pharmaceutical cold-chain claim |','| High-value | 2 W idle lock module target | No access/security authority implemented |','| Fluid | Vented water-like liquid, 90% fill, 0 kPa gauge target | Cryogenic, fuel, chemical and compressed-gas assemblies remain distinct designs |','','## Revision evidence and remaining acceptance','','Each design retains the exact source crop, specifications, editable Blender source with named materials and mechanical parents, neutral GLB, transparent cutout, close/top Blender views, actual Shipyard close/top captures, source/previous/current comparison, measured validation and capture provenance. Open/half-open, underside, stacking/carrier sources and render evidence supplement the current revision. Rejected build/capture attempts remain under `attempts/`; they are not substituted for successful evidence.','','The runtime images come from the actual dashboard Shipyard using isolated Playwright network routes into this unsigned catalog. They are not published placements, live ship installation, native flight-camera acceptance, or proof of implemented container behavior. WebGL2/SwiftShader is the capture backend. Native meshes preserve portable PBR color, metallic, roughness and emission. No voxel visual remesh is involved. No fleet performance or LOD budget is claimed.','','Independent Astra visual/runtime, mechanical and coverage reviews now pass with no further feedback across the exact current collection. All 26 design ledgers are awaiting owner review. [Final review record](cargo-collection/reviews/final-review.json) contains reviewer scope and hashes. Only an explicit owner statement approves an exact design revision and its deliverables; publication requires separate authorization.','','## Reproduce safely','','Use `npm run art:library:cargo -- <fresh isolated cargo job JSON>` with a fresh output revision. `dev.toml` selects Blender. `npm run art:library:cargo:fit` creates local review fixtures. Capture recipes are preserved with the collection; start/inspect services only through managed npm/dev.py commands. Never reuse an existing immutable evidence path. Validation: `npm run check`, `npm run build`, `npm run art:check`, and library hash/crop checks. No authority changes were made, so no database smoke migration is needed.']
lines+=['','## Explicit appearances and reference coverage','','A finish retains the same canonical geometry unless its specification names accessory changes. Each has its own Blender source, materials, GLB, transparent cutout, Blender close/top, actual Shipyard close/top, source comparison, capture provenance and validation in the design revision’s `appearances/` folder. Current hand-lid designs are r003; other main collection designs are r002; fluid and loose extensions are r001. Previous evidence remains preserved.','', 'All 77 targeted source appearances (65 cargo-sheet container crops and 12 modular storage/medical crops) have explicit canonical geometry, finish/accessory or unchanged-reuse evidence. The complete reference membership changes and bounded coverage audit are retained with the collection. Narrow and tiny loose cases are distinct geometries. Rack, tractor-bay and storage-tile references are compositions using these reusable designs; ore, crystals, raw resources and pallets retain their separate design queues.']
lines+=['','## Fluid extension operating assumptions','','| Design | Targets and unresolved ratings |','| --- | --- |']
for j in jobs:
 s=j['specification']
 if s['family'].startswith('fluid-'):lines.append('| '+s['family']+' | '+s['operating']['basis']+' Values: '+json.dumps(s['operating']['values'])+' |')
lines+=['','The extension’s one-high carrier studies do not imply a stacking interface. Cryogenic and compressed-gas pressure ratings remain unresolved; geometric water capacity is not expanded gas delivery capacity. Early specification snapshots retain their contemporary pending-evidence notes; current ledger evidence and this report resolve completed render/variant/review work without rewriting history.']
lines+=['','## Validation and next action','','`npm run check` and `npm run build` passed; the build reports the existing bundle-size warning. `npm run art:check` passed. The library deep audit verified 39 source hashes and 2369 exact crop pixel records plus all revision evidence. Six images added during this task were individually inspected and hash-registered, with detailed crop annotation explicitly pending in the source audit.','', 'Next action is owner review of each exact revision and its evidence. No design, stat or publication approval has been inferred. Use [the continuation prompt](prompts/CONTINUE_CARGO.md) for feedback-driven revisions.']
